  Protobuf push messages (all five packages). The messages of Loki's protobuf
  push API (PushRequest, StreamAdapter, EntryAdapter, LabelPairAdapter) are
  hand-encoded from the field numbers and types of pkg/push/push.proto of
  Grafana Loki v3.7.10:
    https://github.com/grafana/loki/blob/v3.7.10/pkg/push/push.proto
    Copyright Grafana Labs, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
    (an Apache-2.0 exception per Loki LICENSING.md).
  google.protobuf.Timestamp field numbers come from the Protocol Buffers
  well-known types (Copyright Google Inc., BSD-3-Clause). The OTLP log messages
  follow the OpenTelemetry protocol specification (Copyright The OpenTelemetry
  Authors, Apache-2.0). google.rpc.Status (decoded from OTLP error bodies) comes
  from the Google APIs common protos (Copyright Google LLC, Apache-2.0). No code
  was copied from these projects; no Grafana Loki Go module is imported.

  Notable runtime dependencies of the service code: snappyjs (MIT) and ws (MIT)
  for TypeScript; snap (BSD-3-Clause) and tokio-tungstenite (MIT) for Rust;
  github.com/golang/snappy (BSD-3-Clause) and github.com/coder/websocket (ISC)
  for Go; websockets (BSD-3-Clause) and the optional cramjam (MIT) for Python;
  io.airlift:aircompressor (Apache-2.0) for Java.
